---

// Editorial page: fully static, rendered at build time.
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <header class="page-head container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
    <h1>Terms of Use and Disclaimers</h1>
    <p>
      Plain-language ground rules for using this site, written for the site as it actually
      exists. Last updated: <strong>20 October 2026</strong>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section container prose">
    <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      This is an independent, fan-made information site about the Parking Fury series, plus an
      original mini-game written for it. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by
      the games’ creator (Andriy Pidvirnyy), Coolmath Games, Poki, Brain Software, or any other
      platform or rights holder. Nothing on this site should be taken as an official statement by
      any of them.
    </p>

    <h2>2. The games belong to someone else</h2>
    <p>
      “Parking Fury”, “Parking Fury 2”, “Parking Fury 3”, “Parking Fury 3D” and related names and
      game content are the property of their respective owners. This site hosts no copies of those
      games: it links to the platforms that license them, and those platforms’ own terms of
      service and privacy policies apply the moment you follow a link or load their game.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Our content</h2>
    <p>
      The writing, illustrations and the mini-game on this site are original work, © 2026 this
      site’s operator. You are welcome to read, share and link to it freely with attribution.
      Do not copy substantial portions into another site, and do not re-upload the mini-game or
      its code elsewhere as your own.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Personal, non-commercial browsing and playing is fine.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to disrupt, overload or scrape the site, or bypass any security behaviour.</li>
      <li>Do not use the contact channel for spam, harassment or unsolicited marketing.</li>
      <li>Do not frame this site inside another property in a way that misrepresents it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Accuracy — and its limits</h2>
    <p>
      Facts about the games are checked against official host pages and dated where they appear
      (currently October 2026). Game pages, features and availability change without notice, so
      treat this as documentation of a moment, not a guarantee. Where a detail could not be
      verified, it is deliberately absent rather than guessed. The site is provided “as is”, with
      no warranties of any kind, to the extent the law allows.
    </p>

    <h2>6. External links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to third-party platforms are provided for convenience. This site does not control
      those destinations and is not responsible for their content, availability, advertising or
      data practices. If a link leads somewhere unexpected, do not trust it — and
      <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>, because keeping links clean is part of the deal here.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, this site’s operator is not liable for damages
      arising from use of, or inability to use, this site or its guides — including lost game
      progress, device issues originating on third-party sites, or decisions taken on the basis of
      a guide. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot legally be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated as the site changes; the date above moves with them. Continued
      use after an update means acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms, licensing conversations, or takedown notices go through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Background on how the site is run is on the
      <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
